I need to know how to lookup a pack from this contract which has been unpacked but is pending to be claimed?
To lookup a pack that has been unboxed but is still pending to be claimed on the atomicpacksx contract, follow these steps using a WAX block explorer like WAX Block or Bloks.io:

Locate Pending Results in the Contract Tables
The atomicpacksx contract stores pending results in two specific tables after a user transfers a pack NFT with the memo unbox:
unboxassets table: This table contains the actual template IDs of the NFTs you pulled. To find your pending items, you must use the Asset ID of the original pack you transferred as the Scope for this table.
unboxpacks table: This table stores general metadata for the opened pack. An entry remains here until all individual roll results have been claimed.
How to Lookup on a Block Explorer
Go to the atomicpacksx contract page on a block explorer.
Navigate to the Contract tab and then the Tables sub-tab.
Select the unboxassets table from the dropdown menu.
In the Scope field, enter the Asset ID of the pack you opened.
If results appear, they represent the NFTs waiting to be claimed. Note the origin_roll_id for each entry (usually starting at 0).
Claiming the Pending Pack
Once you have identified the pending results, you can manually claim them using the claimunboxed action:
Navigate to the Actions tab on the atomicpacksx contract page.
Select the claimunboxed action.
Enter the following details:
claimer: Your WAX wallet address.
pack_asset_id: The Asset ID of the pack you opened.
origin_roll_ids: A list of the roll IDs found in the unboxassets table (e.g., [0, 1, 2] if there were three items in the pack).
