✅ FIXED! The Real Issue with Claimable Packs
You were 100% RIGHT! The problem was that I was only checking packs the user OWNS, but once they're unpacked, they're in the atomicpacksx contract, not the user's wallet!

🔍 What Was Wrong
Before:

Only queried AtomicAssets API for packs user owns
Once unpacked (transferred to atomicpacksx), packs disappeared from owned list
System tried to unpack already-unpacked packs → "Sender doesn't own" error
The Missing Piece:

Unpacked but unclaimed packs live in atomicpacksx::unboxpacks table
These packs have roll data in atomicpacksx::unboxassets table
We weren't checking this table at all!
🛠️ What I Fixed
1. New Backend Endpoint (server.js:1617-1710)

GET /api/user/claimable-packs/:account

Queries atomicpacksx::unboxpacks table using secondary index (unlock_account)
Finds all packs unpacked by the user but not yet claimed
For each pack, fetches roll IDs from unboxassets table
Returns complete list with roll counts
2. Updated Frontend (packs.js:242-312)

Now fetches TWO lists:
Owned packs (from AtomicAssets API)
Claimable packs (from atomicpacksx unboxpacks table)
Combines both lists for display
Claimable packs show orange "🎁 Claim Contents" button
Owned packs show green "📦 Unpack" button
