The Problem
In the server.js code (lines 1776-1783), I was using:

lower_bound: packAssetId,
upper_bound: packAssetId,  // ❌ BUG HERE

In EOSIO/WAX blockchain table queries, upper_bound is EXCLUSIVE. When you set lower_bound and upper_bound to the same value, the query range is empty and returns no rows!

The Fix
Changed to:

lower_bound: packAssetId,
// No upper_bound - just use limit 1

And added verification to ensure we got the correct asset:

if (assetResult.rows && assetResult.rows.length > 0 && assetResult.rows[0].asset_id === packAssetId) {
  templateMint = assetResult.rows[0].template_mint;
}

