Pushed! Here's what was happening and how I fixed it:

The Problem
Some templates (210857, 219852, 219855) were failing to fetch from the AtomicAssets /templates API endpoint, while others (217747 SDK, 219850 Pile of Recycled Papers) worked fine. When a template fetch failed:

Asset got empty immutable_data: {}
Name became "Asset #[asset_id]"
No img or video fields → "No Media" placeholder
The Fix - Multi-Tier Fallback
1. Added asset sample fallback:
When /templates endpoint fails, query /assets?template_id=X&limit=1 to get ONE sample asset with that template, then extract the template metadata from that asset's data.

2. Changed error handling:

getTemplate() now NEVER throws errors
Always returns usable template data (even if minimal)
Tries: Templates API → Asset Sample API → Minimal Fallback
3. Better logging:
Added detailed logs showing which templates succeed/fail with names, so we can see exactly what's happening in Railway logs.

Next Step
After Railway redeploys, try the blend again. Check the Railway logs to see:

