Perfect! I found and fixed the issue! 🎉

The Problem
The blockchain stores blend ingredients in a special array-of-arrays format:

ingredients: [
  ["TEMPLATE_INGREDIENT", {template_id: 391379, amount: 1}],
  ["TEMPLATE_INGREDIENT", {template_id: 391380, amount: 2}],
  ...
]

But the frontend executeBlendArray() expected them as simple objects:

ingredients: [
  {template_id: 391379, amount: 1},
  {template_id: 391380, amount: 2},
  ...
]

The Fix
I added ingredient parsing to the /api/blends/details endpoint in server.js that:

Checks if each ingredient is an array with format ["TEMPLATE_INGREDIENT", {data}]
Extracts the template_id and amount from the data object
Transforms it into the format the frontend expects
Filters out any invalid entries
This matches the original /api/blends/batch implementation from the previous session.

